infiltrator-software (0.3.10) unstable; urgency=high

  * Enable Discover installation instead of permanently presenting the
    transaction-planner placeholder.
  * Resolve native install/update dependency graphs asynchronously and show the
    complete package change set before requesting administrator authorization.
  * Fall back to the transitional APT planner when a shared native generation is
    not yet available, while still prohibiting package removal.
  * Execute every approved install/upgrade plan item at its exact reviewed
    version and disable implicit Recommends/Suggests in the privileged bridge.
  * Make Updates execute the exact resolved plan rather than reconstructing a
    second root-only transaction after confirmation.
  * Refresh Discover, Installed and Updates state after a successful install.
  * Add CI regression checks preventing Discover installation from being
    silently disabled again.

